            <ArticleTitle>Perforation of Meckel's diverticulum by a chicken bone, a rare complication: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>606-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A perforation of Meckel's diverticulum by foreign bodies is an extremely rare cause of acute abdomen in adults. We herein present a case of a 30-year-old man who was admitted due to symptoms of right lower quadrant pain, anorexia, and vomiting. An exploratory laparotomy was done, and a perforated Meckel's diverticulum due to a chicken bone was found at exploration. A resection of a segment of ileum including the perforated diverticulum was performed, and the patient had an uncomplicated postoperative course.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
